7. Query Processing Design

The legal assistant follows this process:

User enters question
        ↓
Text preprocessing
        ↓
Identify keywords/context
        ↓
Legal category detection
        ↓
Retrieve relevant information
        ↓
Generate simple explanation
        ↓
Display answer + official resources
8. Security Design

Security is important because users may enter sensitive information.

The system should include:

Secure login
Password hashing
Input validation
Access control
HTTPS
Secure database access
Minimal collection of personal information
Protection against unauthorized access
9. Design Principles

The Legalease design should follow these principles:

Simple – Easy for non-technical users.
Accessible – Information should be understandable.
Reliable – Prefer verified and official legal sources.
Transparent – Show sources and update dates.
Secure – Protect user information.
Responsive – Work on computers and mobile devices.
Responsible AI – Clearly distinguish general information from professional legal advice.
10. Final Design Outcome

The Project Design Phase produces the blueprint for the Legalease system. It defines the interface, modules, database, architecture, security, and information flow before actual development begins. This design provides a clear foundation for the next stage: Project Development/Implementation.
